1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:05,940
One dream, one wish If you want it,

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:08,260
gotta go over the top!

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,380
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

6
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,857
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

7
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:41,417
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,200
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

9
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,457
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

10
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:56,420
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

11
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,537
Despite all that to run is not an option.

12
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:01,637
Once they're closed, I
feel the satisfaction.

13
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

14
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,040
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,317
If you are going on your way.

16
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,737
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

18
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,257
Yes, I can.

19
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:22,077
As you're on your way.

20
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,337
Marks maps will be made.

21
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,197
Yes, with every step that you will take.

22
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

23
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead at new horizons.

24
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,977
In view shining brightly.

25
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,860
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you.

26
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,137
Dream living, that's the way.

27
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:42,177
Make like a hurricane.

28
00:01:42,260 --> 00:01:45,100
Now, got to make your mark today.

29
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,977
One dream, one wish.

30
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

31
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,937
Go for the knockout.

32
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,000
Over the top!

33
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:12,420
This is bad!

34
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:14,900
Go back to the mountain without me!

35
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,280
Are you sure, sir?

36
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,740
Things are about to get ugly.

37
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,140
I know that much.

38
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:29,060
Even for him, this is terrifying.

39
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:32,460
And it was over in a flash.

40
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,094
I'd hoped it would take long
enough for him to sober up.

41
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,400
Get back here!

42
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,780
He's right here!

43
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,340
Run!

44
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:51,560
No!

45
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,880
No!

46
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:07,400
Dammit! My house! My house!

47
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:08,780
Daddy!

48
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,900
Third gear! Let's go!

49
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,880
Let's go!

50
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:24,140
I've got to stop Kaido right
now, so I can't hold back!

51
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:34,500
Gum-Gum Elephant Guys!

52
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:49,820
Oh, my God.

53
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:13,336
Something knocked him out of the sky!

54
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,217
Who the hell is that?

55
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:38,340
Wait, I know him!

56
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:40,677
It's the guy who took out a rash man!

57
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:41,760
General Hold 'em!

58
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,330
Kiku!

59
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,680
I remain unharmed.

60
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,280
And you, Master?

61
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,197
I'm fine.

62
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,257
I feared I'd lost you.

63
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:06,860
That fear is unfounded.

64
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,240
But the others...

65
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:27,640
Odin Castle! No!

66
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:35,680
Lord Momonosuke!

67
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:42,460
Wait, Master Keen.

68
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:43,840
Wait for what?

69
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:46,060
Without him, it's all for nothing.

70
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:49,320
I must ensure his safety,
no matter the cost.

71
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,660
I feel the same.

72
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,820
It's not that.

73
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:53,517
It's just...

74
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:57,071
I think there is someone else
you should be worrying about.

75
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,330
Tsuru

76
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:05,137
Karoo could wake up and continue
his rampage at any moment.

77
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,797
The townspeople are still in grave danger.

78
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:11,177
A fine point.

79
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:13,397
Then I shall go to Okobori town.

80
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:16,677
And I shall leave the young
lord in your capable hands.

81
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,060
Very well!

82
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:34,580
You made it out.

83
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:37,660
You survived that somehow. Right, guys?

84
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,000
General Speed!

85
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:42,740
What happened?

86
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,528
Those are serious injuries.

87
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,582
I thought she left town earlier.

88
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:51,120
I thought so too, but I just saw
her fall from the commander's body.

89
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,620
Speed, say something, please!

90
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,240
Who the hell are you?

91
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,600
Hey, what happened to you?

92
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,350
Porcelina!

93
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,720
No, General Speed!

94
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:07,920
Wait a second!

95
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:13,557
What the heck are you doing
here in the first place?

96
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:14,480
Where's Tama?

97
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:17,191
Please tell me you got her back home safe!

98
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:22,617
Say something! Come on!

99
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:28,000
On our way back, we were
spotted by Commander Kaido.

100
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:35,037
I tried my best to fight, but
I couldn't protect her. I...

101
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:37,560
I failed my master.

102
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,000
Where do you think you're going, Speed?

103
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,840
I'm scared!

104
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:20,560
I received a very
troubling report about you.

105
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:52,120
Damn it!

106
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:55,740
I shouldn't have left her!

107
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,280
I should have protected her!

108
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,831
There you are, Straw Hat!

109
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:06,157
What the hell are you doing with her?

110
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,070
We should run!

111
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:09,062
You got a lucky shot back there.

112
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,697
And Kaido's so big he
probably didn't notice you.

113
00:11:11,780 --> 00:11:14,486
It's not too late to get
the hell out of here!

114
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:15,980
Kaido got to Tama.

115
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:19,000
You saw what he did.

116
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:22,393
Kinemon's friends and both of our crews.

117
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:24,900
We don't know if they're alive

118
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:29,780
But if I kick his ass
now, it's over, right?

119
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:36,620
Come fight me Kaido!

120
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,360
I'm right here!

121
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:21,660
The man who's going to
be King of the Pirates!

122
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,200
Last breath!

123
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:10,980
So at last, you've come
to the land of Wano!

124
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:13,240
Time for third gear!

125
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,420
Aaaaaaah!

126
00:13:29,920 --> 00:13:32,140
Aaaaaaah! Yeah!

127
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:45,980
Aaaaaaah!

128
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,760
You just couldn't resist.

129
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,282
As soon as you get here,
you screw everything up.

130
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:16,810
No!

131
00:15:03,660 --> 00:15:06,860
Now come back!

132
00:15:15,980 --> 00:15:18,977
I just wanted to tell you that
I'll never forget this big

133
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:22,589
brew because I've never had
such good food in my whole life.

134
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:29,380
I can't love you!

135
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,240
AAAAAAUGH!

136
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:51,960
AAAAAAAAH!

137
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:25,160
I don't know.

138
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:14,937
I'll set you flying!

139
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,680
FLYING KIDO!

140
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:25,850
HONKAM!

141
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:29,850
FRIZLY!

142
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:32,320
MAGNUS!

143
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,100
No!

144
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:37,440
Oh, my God.

145
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,980
4th gear! Bounce man!

146
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:05,840
Time to finish this!

147
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:20,400
You've screwed up this country enough!

148
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:25,000
Now that you've messed
with my friends, it's over!

149
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:38,840
Kong Kong!

150
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:42,320
Kong Kong!

151
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:51,540
Ahhhhhhhhhhh!

152
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:31,520
Now, Kum-Kum!

153
00:20:33,660 --> 00:20:36,197
Double-tubbering!

154
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:37,986
What, what, what, what, what?

155
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:44,620
Tom, Tom!

156
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:53,680
Tom Morgan, die!

157
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:17,720
Oh, my God.

158
00:21:57,820 --> 00:22:00,200
This guy's a monster, but who is he?

159
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,840
Oh, my God.

160
00:23:00,160 --> 00:23:03,080
He can't die!

161
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:10,500
Thundermar!

162
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:47,140
I don't know.

163
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:19,200
That useless idiot!

164
00:24:29,320 --> 00:24:31,040
I can't believe this.

165
00:24:31,180 --> 00:24:32,415
He's still breathing.

166
00:24:34,220 --> 00:24:36,100
Of course he is.

167
00:24:37,060 --> 00:24:41,220
I don't know if this is a show
of will or simply bravado,

168
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:45,780
but that little bastard's glaring at me.

169
00:24:57,060 --> 00:24:57,890
Glaring?

170
00:24:57,973 --> 00:24:59,597
You've got good eyes, Commander.

171
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:01,268
He looks knocked out to me.

172
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:23,220
What was that you said about being king?

173
00:25:25,180 --> 00:25:26,980
You're nothing.
